<%#
  Diagnostics (the brief, §11 and §12). The page whose whole job is to be honest about the difference between
  "a credential works" and "an invoice can be created and posted".

  Both buttons are POSTs. The connection test authenticates against a third-party server; the capability probe
  creates a document in it. Neither is something a link somebody pastes should be able to do.
%>
<% content_for(:title) do %>Odoo diagnostics<% end %>

<header class="main-content__header" role="banner">
  <h1 class="main-content__page-title" id="page-title">Odoo Accounting</h1>
</header>

<section class="main-content__body">
  <%= render 'tabs' %>

  <% if @profile.nil? %>
    <%= render 'empty_state', message: '' %>
  <% else %>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
      <div class="border border-slate-100 rounded-md p-4">
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-1">1. Connection test</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">
          Reads the server version <em>without</em> credentials, then makes one authenticated read. It proves
          the API key is valid and the user can see <code>account.move</code>.
          <strong>It does not prove an invoice can be created or posted.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mb-3">
          Last run:
          <strong><%= @profile.last_connection_test_at.present? ? l(@profile.last_connection_test_at, format: :long) : 'never' %></strong>
        </p>
        <% if @profile.last_connection_result.present? %>
          <pre class="text-xs bg-slate-25 border border-slate-100 rounded p-3 overflow-x-auto mb-3"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@profile.last_connection_result) %></pre>
        <% end %>
        <%= button_to 'Run connection test', test_connection_super_admin_odoo_accounting_path,
                      class: 'px-3 py-2 text-sm rounded bg-woot-500 text-white hover:bg-woot-600' %>
      </div>

      <div class="border border-slate-100 rounded-md p-4">
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-1">2. Capability probe</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mb-3">
          Six independent checks: the shape of <code>account.move</code> on this server, the company, the sales
          journal's type and company, the payment journal, the analytic account if one is configured, and
          finally <strong>one draft invoice created in the configured journal, read back, and deleted</strong>.
          A draft has no sequence number, so deleting it leaves no accounting trace and no gap in your numbering.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm mb-3">
          Last run:
          <strong><%= @profile.last_capability_proof_at.present? ? l(@profile.last_capability_proof_at, format: :long) : 'never' %></strong>
        </p>
        <% if @profile.last_capability_proof.present? %>
          <pre class="text-xs bg-slate-25 border border-slate-100 rounded p-3 overflow-x-auto mb-3"><%= JSON.pretty_generate(@profile.last_capability_proof) %></pre>
        <% end %>
        <%= button_to 'Run capability probe', run_capability_probe_super_admin_odoo_accounting_path,
                      class: 'px-3 py-2 text-sm rounded bg-woot-500 text-white hover:bg-woot-600' %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="border border-amber-200 bg-amber-25 rounded-md p-4 max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-1">3. Posting is not proven, and is not claimed to be</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-700">
        Posting an invoice gives it a permanent number from your journal's sequence and cannot be undone
        &mdash; a posted invoice is reversed, never deleted. There is therefore no way to probe posting without
        leaving a real document in your books, so this integration does not try, and does not pretend the
        probe above covers it.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-700 mt-2">
        What that means in practice: leave <strong>Post invoices automatically</strong> off until you have
        exported a few real invoices as drafts and posted one yourself in Odoo. The first invoice that posts
        successfully is the real test. Until then every export is a draft, which is reversible by deleting it.
      </p>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
